Ampere front end (NVN2): a bindless texture whose handle the draw determines (constants, constant buffer words, storage buffer words at
such offsets: the material texture tables of NVN2 games) becomes an ordinary texture binding with constant buffer slot HandleExprSlot
(0x20000); the handle expression goes to the accessor log as "handle-expr n rpn" and the runtime evaluates it at each draw. Tried after
the constant buffer patterns, before the pool array. A comparison sample that cannot be bound answers 1 (lit) instead of 0. The
Ryujinx code in the context lines is MIT.
